<title>PHILIPPINES: PCI Leasing debuts at 7.60 pesos.</title>
<headline>PCI Leasing debuts at 7.60 pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>PCI Leasing and Finance Inc made its debut on the Philippine Stock Exchange on Monday at 7.60 pesos, up from its offering price of 6.95 pesos, brokers said.</p>
<p>Trading volume was moderate at 1.788 million shares.  </p>
<p>&quot;Prospects of the company are good because it is the biggest financing and leasing company in the Philippines,&quot; one broker said.</p>
<p>The leasing firm, a unit of Philippine Commercial International Bank, had offered 121 million shares.</p>
<p>In a presentation at the launch of the IPO, PCI Leasing officials had said they expected the firm's net income to grow by at least 30 percent annually over the next five years.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (632) 841 8934</p>
</text>
